## Highlights in `{{RELEASE_TAG}}`

- **Automatic SoundCloud Go+ High Quality (`256 kbps` AAC-LC @ `44.1 kHz`)**: Uses your existing `soundcloud.com` browser session with **zero separate login** and **zero disk-stored credentials**, automatically upgrading SoundCloud Web's default `sq` stream to `hq` (`aac_256k`) when available—including private and secret-link tracks. Also works seamlessly with SoundCloud Free and signed-out browsing.
- **Direct Denon & Marantz HEOS Network Streaming (`0 dB` `44.1 kHz / 24-bit` Lossless FLAC)**:
  - Automatic SSDP/mDNS/HEOS discovery on your home LAN with zero IP configuration.
  - **Hands-Free Auto-Wake**: Pressing **Play** on `soundcloud.com` automatically wakes your Denon/Marantz amplifier from Network Standby and switches to **HEOS Music**.
  - **Front OLED Track Metadata & Exact Duration**: Streams uncompressed RFC 9639 `24-bit / 44.1 kHz` FLAC with `VORBIS_COMMENT` & `DIDL-Lite` tags so your amplifier's front display shows the live **Track Title**, **Artist**, and **Elapsed / Total Time** while preventing unintended EU Auto-Standby shutdowns during playback.
- **Bit-Perfect Optical TOSLINK Mode (`44.1 kHz` S/PDIF)**: Locks macOS CoreAudio physical sample rate to `44,100 Hz` at `0 dB` unity gain with continuous silent S/PDIF optical clock lock (`anullsrc`) to eliminate DAC relock clicks between tracks.
- **Strict Amp-Knob-Only Volume (`0 dB` Invariant)**: SoundClud never attenuates digital samples and never sends remote volume commands to your amplifier—your physical Hi-Fi volume knob and remote remain in 100% control.
- **Multi-Hour DJ Mix Resilience & Instant Waveform Scrubbing**: Transparently refreshes expiring SoundCloud HLS CDN signatures mid-mix (`HTTP 403` recovery) and supports instant `HTTP 206` byte-range waveform seeking across 1–4+ hour sets.
- **Graceful Widevine DRM Local Fallback**: If an individual major-label track requires hardware Widevine DRM, SoundClud plays that single track locally in your browser and automatically resumes Hi-Fi handoff on the very next track in your queue.

